## F4 - ETF trend study module, tests and script (no real run)

- **Date:** 2026-11-24
- **Task:** F4 - implement ETF trend study module, synthetic tests, and study script for H-17. No real run, no snapshot read/compute beyond code/tests.
- **What changed and why:** Added `backend/app/research/etf_trend.py` with pure/no-network functions per frozen spec: `load_snapshot` (verifies sha256 vs manifest, raises on mismatch), `signal_dates`, `eligible_assets`, `momentum_12_1`, `trend_pass`, `target_weights` (defaults frozen), `simulate` (s+1 execution, weight drift, cost on execution day), `metrics` (CAGR, Sharpe ddof=1*sqrt(252), MaxDD negative, Calmar, annual turnover, share of days in SHY), `paired_month_bootstrap(strategy, benchmark, n=2000, seed=17000)`, `tier_flags`. Added `backend/tests/test_research_etf_trend.py` with 12 synthetic deterministic tests covering the F4-required cases: look-ahead, weights sum 1, <253 bars ineligible, below 200d mean -> SHY, alphabetical ties, s+1 execution timing, cost hand-computed, zero turnover zero cost, tier_flags boundaries/equal not Tier B pass, bootstrap deterministic/CI contains point estimate, load_snapshot raises on byte change. Added `scripts/research_etf_trend.py` with frozen defaults, required `--snapshot-dir`, `--prereg` default H-17 prereg, `--report`, `--json-dir`, dirty-tree refusal unless `--allow-dirty` (same guard approach as run_research_baseline.py), primary + 7 descriptive comparators on dev/holdout windows, and report including Tier A/B four-way label, point estimates/CIs, comparator table, per-year table, 2008/2020/2022 drawdowns, frozen limits text. Updated `.github/workflows/research.yml` to include new test in pytest and new script in ruff.
- **Files touched:**
  - `backend/app/research/etf_trend.py` (created)
  - `backend/tests/test_research_etf_trend.py` (created)
  - `scripts/research_etf_trend.py` (created)
  - `.github/workflows/research.yml` (edited)
  - `docs/SESSIONS/research-etf-log.nd` (appended)

